#%PAM-1.0
# Host-oriented sketch ONLY — not installed by the demo image and not applied
# to any live Lightsail / dogfood host by this repository.
#
# Intent (fail-closed MFA with named break-glass):
#   - Interactive users: primary factor (pubkey or unix) AND pam_ezkey required.
#   - Named break-glass account skips pam_ezkey (console / emergency access).
#   - Never put pam_ezkey on a path that locks root console without a tested bypass.
#   - Do NOT enable Duo-style failmode=safe inside pam_ezkey.
#   - Keep pam_ezkey as required/requisite. PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL is fail-closed only
#     with those controls; sufficient or [default=ignore] makes MFA fail-open.
#   - Use https:// Integration API URL; leave lab_http=false on the host conf.
#
# Contrast with the demo stack in ./sshd (Ezkey-only + pam_permit): that stack is
# valid only for the disposable Docker SSH VM.
#
# Example sketch (adapt user names, order, and account module to the host):
#
# auth       [success=1 default=ignore] pam_succeed_if.so user = breakglass quiet
# auth       required     pam_unix.so
# auth       required     pam_ezkey.so conf=/etc/security/pam_ezkey.conf
# auth       required     pam_permit.so
#
# Or with SSH publickey as the first factor (sshd_config AuthenticationMethods
# publickey,keyboard-interactive:pam) and pam_ezkey as the MFA line:
#
# auth       required     pam_ezkey.so conf=/etc/security/pam_ezkey.conf
# account    required     pam_unix.so
# session    required     pam_unix.so
#
# sshd_config (host): LoginGraceTime >= 120.
#
# MANDATORY — MaxAuthTries 1 inside Match (not global).
# OpenSSH portable forks each keyboard-interactive PAM round and _exit's — each
# prompt round is one pam_sm_authenticate and one Integration API auth request.
# A pam_set_data marker does NOT stop a second create after Deny/Expire (#907).
# Edgar retest of #908 (2026-10-20): F9 (one SSH login → 3 auth requests) is
# fixed only when MaxAuthTries 1 is inside the MFA Match; leave other users
# (e.g. ec2-user) on the global try budget. Prefer Match Group over a global
# MaxAuthTries 1 (refused public keys also consume tries):
#
# Match Group ezkey-mfa
#     MaxAuthTries 1
#     AuthenticationMethods keyboard-interactive
#     PubkeyAuthentication no
#
# Single-user lab alternative:
# Match User mfa-user
#     MaxAuthTries 1
#     AuthenticationMethods keyboard-interactive
#     PubkeyAuthentication no
#
# WARNING: without this Match, OpenSSH recreates auth attempts after Deny/Expire
# in the same TCP connection (#907 F9). Do not rely on PAM_MAXTRIES across rounds.
#
# Clients: ssh -o NumberOfPasswordPrompts=1 …
#
# Rollback: restore /etc/pam.d/sshd from a copy taken the same day; sshd -t before
# restart. Confirm Lightsail serial/browser console the same day as any cutover.
# Never commit origin IPs — use <static-ip ezkey-online-community> in notes.
